       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. WVLOAD.
      *****************************************************************
      * A FLAT BUFFER, THEN AN 01 THAT REDEFINES IT WITH A TYPED     *
      * LAYOUT OF TWO 03 GROUPS.  Shop-style quirks on purpose:      *
      *  - the 01 lines are typed in column 1 (level in the seq area)*
      *  - WV-DATA's PICTURE is pushed past column 72                *
      *  - each 05 carries its PICTURE on the next line              *
      * The changing field is in the SECOND 03.  The trace must      *
      * climb 05 -> 03 -> 01, cross the REDEFINES, and judge WV-DATA *
      * (4096 bytes) already big enough - a note, not a change.      *
      *****************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
           EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
           EXEC SQL BEGIN DECLARE SECTION END-EXEC.
01           WV-DATA                                                  PIC X(4096).
01           WV-CUTBLA-VIEW REDEFINES WV-DATA.
           03  WV-CUTBLA-HDR.
               05  WV-REC-TYPE
                               PIC X(02).
               05  WV-REC-SEQ
                               PIC 9(06).
           03  WV-CUTBLA-KEY.
               05  WV-VALUE
                               PIC S9(10)V9(2).
               05  WV-CUST-NAME
                               PIC X(30).
           EXEC SQL END DECLARE SECTION END-EXEC.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       0000-MAIN.
           EXEC SQL
               SELECT CB_VALUE, CB_NAME
                 INTO :WV-VALUE, :WV-CUST-NAME
                 FROM CUTBLA
                WHERE CB_ID = 1
           END-EXEC
           STOP RUN.
